--- !u!114 &1741145791
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 1741145790}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: b096626d39e2f7dd882348b9cb85cb8b, type: 3}
  m_Name: 
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::GlorifiedBody.Interaction.InWorldScreen
  range: 1.6
  point: {fileID: 1110535267}
  clip: {fileID: 0}
  faces:
  - {fileID: 676400053}
  lines:
  - at: 0.5
    speaker: CABAL
    text: There! There they go! That faint gleam of light.
  - at: 4.54
    speaker: PASSWORTHY
    text: I feel that what we've done is monstrous!
  - at: 8.195
    speaker: CABAL
    text: What they've done is magnificent.
  - at: 11.41
    speaker: PASSWORTHY
    text: Will they come back?
  - at: 13.91
    speaker: CABAL
    text: Yes, and go again and again, until the landing is made and the moon is
      conquered. This is only a beginning.
  - at: 21.195
    speaker: PASSWORTHY
    text: But if they don't come back, my son and your daughter, what of that, Cabal?
  - at: 26.72
    speaker: CABAL
    text: Then presently others will go.
  - at: 29.769999
    speaker: PASSWORTHY
    text: Oh God, is there ever to be any age of happiness? Is there never to be
      any rest?
  - at: 35.57
    speaker: CABAL
    text: Rest enough for the individual man. Too much and too soon, and we call
      it death. But for Man, no rest and no ending. He must go on, conquest beyond
      conquest.
  - at: 42.97
    speaker: CABAL
    text: First this little planet and its winds and ways, and then all the laws
      of mind and matter that restrain him.
  - at: 50.31
    speaker: CABAL
    text: Then the planets about it, and at last out across immensity to the stars.
  - at: 55.725002
    speaker: CABAL
    text: And when he has conquered all the deeps of space and all the mysteries
      of time, still he will be beginning.
  - at: 63.010002
    speaker: PASSWORTHY
    text: But we're such little creatures. Our humanity is so fragile, so weak. Little
      animals.
  - at: 69.085
    speaker: CABAL
    text: Little animals. And if we're no more than animals, we must snatch each
      little scrap of happiness and live and suffer and pass, mattering no more than
      all the other animals do or have done.
  - at: 76.485
    speaker: CABAL
    text: It is this, or that. All the universe or nothingness. Which shall it be,
      Passworthy? Which shall it be?
  - at: 83.55
    speaker: 
    text: '[The end credits roll: the names of an animation staff, fast and small,
      white on black.]'
  - at: 89.79
    speaker: 
    text: "\xA9 THE TECHNOPURITAN CHURCH. ALL RIGHTS RESERVED."
  interactive: 0
  loop: 0
  hearing: 12
  volume: 1
  ducksMusic: 1
  pausesTape: 1
  thing: the screen
